<h2>Segment 217 &mdash; the stream and the basis for seeds</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s217S">&#x27;o na <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w1">&#x27;jug &#x27;grel</span> las, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w2">sems</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w3">rgyun</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w4">bag chags</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w5">gzhir</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w6">gsungs pa</span> ji ltar yin zhe na, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w7">nga</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w8">tsam</span> de nyid <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w9">sems</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w10">rnam shes</span> la brten nas <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s217w11">btags pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w12">rgyud</span> yin pas, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w13">sems</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w14">rgyud</span> ces <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w15">kyang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w16">bya</span> la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w17">sems</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w18">nyid</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w19">rigs <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s217w20">&#x27;dra</span></span> la de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w21">rgyud</span> ces pa ltar na, de <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w22">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w23">res &#x27;ga&#x27; ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w24">bag chags</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w25">sgo ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w26">gzhir</span> &#x27;gyur ro</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s217S">One may ask the following: The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w1">autocommentary to Entering the Middle Way</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w6">states</span> that the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w3">stream</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w2">mind</span> is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w5">basis</span> where the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w4">mental seeds</span> are planted. How does this fit into what you have just said? The very thing we call the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w8">simple</span> &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w7">me</span>&quot; is something which results from a <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s217w11">label being applied</span> to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w9">mind</span>, or <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w10">consciousness</span>. It also goes on in a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w12">stream</span>. From this point of view then we can <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w15">also</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w16">refer</span> to it as the &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w14">stream</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w13">mind</span>.&quot; And even if what you mean by a &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w21">stream</span>&quot; is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w19">continuation of later, <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s217w20">similar</span> instances</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w17">mind</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w18">itself</span>, you can say that it <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s217w22">too</span> is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w26">basis</span> which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w25">stained</span> by <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w24">mental seeds</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s217w23">particular occasions</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment proposed by Codex, Tibetan-first; future proposal only. The four mind/stream occurrences are separately placed with explicit English order. The established compound rigs 'dra takes the attested continuation-of-similar-instances rendering, with only 'dra → similar as a member. btags pa is retained at phrase depth for the passive label-being-applied recast; brten nas and the surrounding explanatory causal framing are omitted as distributed. gzhir retains its bound terminative ending while basis alone is matched. Supplied participants, articles, planted, later explanatory scaffolding, and unresolved recasts remain unwrapped; no null asserts absence where correspondence is uncertain. HGM glossary and other corpus renderings are distinguished in saved evidence; nothing changes hgm_gloss.</div>
